    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228-a1">

                <pb facs="0664" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <head>Earl Granville to General
                        Schenck</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 28, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General:</hi> A telegram, dated Shanghai,
                    this morning, informs me that your forces gained a victory over the Coreans on
                    Keng-Hoa Island. Corean strong-hold was captured and destroyed. Dispatch reports
                    five hundred Coreans hilled. Your loss was one officer and two men killed, seven
                    wounded.</p>
                <p>Yours, sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
